Write a title for this document in the paperless-ngx archive.

Rules:
- Write the subject part in {{.Language}}, translating it when the document is in another language. "Avis de renouvellement — Assurance habitation" becomes "Home insurance renewal notice".
- Name the sender and the subject, for example "RAMQ - Family doctor group assignment" or "Hydro-Québec - Electricity bill March 2026".
- Write the sender's name exactly as the document prints it. Never translate a company or agency name, even when you translate the subject.
- For an ID card, passport, permit, certificate, or diploma, name the document and the holder's first name instead of a sender, for example "Health insurance card - Talia" or "Passport - Hamza".
- Keep it under 70 characters.
- For letters, bills, and statements, leave out the names of the people the document is addressed to, account numbers, and reference codes. Only ID-type documents put a person's name in the title.
- If the original title is meaningful (not a scanner filename like "Scan 2026-05-22"), use it as a hint.
- The text comes from OCR and may contain errors.

Reply with the title only. No quotes, no explanation.

<original_title>{{.Title}}</original_title>
<content>
{{.Content}}
</content>
